  "confidence": 0.82,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": [
        "C14"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "C14-1",
        "C14-2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "+3V3",
        "NET0030"
      ],
      "observed": "C14 is a 100 nF capacitor connected between the +3V3 power rail and NET0030, the ESP32-C6 IO1 / FLOAT_HIGH net that also drives the ATO-valve hardware interlock transistor T7.",
      "expected": "A filter/decoupling capacitor on this signal should be connected to GND, as the corresponding FLOAT_LOW filter capacitor C42 is, or should not be present at all. A GPIO/sensor interlock net should not be AC-coupled to a power rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"76\") (name \"NET0030\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C14\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C14\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C14 NET0030 +3V3 100n"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C42 0 NET0075 100n"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FLOAT_HIGH/IO1 node is capacitively tied to +3V3 instead of ground. This can couple supply noise into the high-level water sensor input and alter float-switch transition timing, potentially causing false high-level detection or unintended disabling of the ATO valve through the T7 interlock path.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show an unintended 100 nF capacitor from +3V3 to the FLOAT_HIGH/IO1 net, unlike the matching FLOAT_LOW filter capacitor to ground; this signal-to-rail AC bridge can corrupt high-level water sensing and valve interlock behavior."
}

